From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:40:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] flashnext: the hcn kernels split into their own fatbin
 and the comments read one line

The lean gate holds every touched source at 600 lines and one-line comments: the hcn block moves to
flashnext_hcn.cu (its own fatbin, TileKernels loads it beside flashnext_hcf), the write-back and the
shared-direct dispatch collapse into cuda_batch_hc helpers so cuda_batch.zig stays under the cap, and
the multi-line comments read one line a paragraph.
